h","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" nodes that flip the shape between its base and an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enlarged state; the switch state feeds a ","type":"text"},{"code":"builtin.point3D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" Transform Scale, and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the pop is animated with a spring. At rest the shape sits at base scale on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"magenta artboard."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction_PinchView","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction_PinchView","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Swami","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami"}}}